  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: Path traversal in the AD GPO provider allows writing\n     files outside the GPO cache directory as root\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-14476.patch: reject \"..\" components of\n       gPCFileSysPath in ad_gpo_extract_smb_components() in\n       src/providers/ad/ad_gpo.c and check that the resolved cache path\n       stays inside GPO_CACHE_PATH in gpo_cache_store_file() in\n       src/providers/ad/ad_gpo_child.c\n     - CVE-2026-14476\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Unrestricted LDAP sudo search base allows injecting\n     sudoRole objects granting root privileges\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-14474.patch: warn when ldap_sudo_search_base\n       is not set and the whole directory tree is searched in\n       sdap_set_config_options_with_rootdse() in src/providers/ldap/sdap.c\n     - CVE-2026-14474\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Privilege escalation via the Kerberos an2ln localauth\n     fallback on AD/IPA clients\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2025-11561.patch: disable the an2ln localauth\n       plugin in the SSSD localauth plugin configuration snippet in\n       src/util/domain_info_utils.c\n     - CVE-2025-11561",
